 "title": "AB and BA move the square differently",
 "caption": "Apply the matrices to the unit square. AB = [[2, 1], [1, 1]] sends it to one parallelogram and BA = [[1, 1], [1, 2]] to another, so AB ≠ BA. Both have determinant 1, so both keep the area.",
 "alt": "The unit square and its two images: AB gives a parallelogram with vertices (0, 0), (2, 1), (3, 2), (1, 1); BA gives (0, 0), (1, 1), (2, 3), (1, 2).",
 "description": [
  "The unit square is the starting shape.",
  "AB = [[2, 1], [1, 1]] sends the corners to (0, 0), (2, 1), (3, 2), (1, 1).",
  "BA = [[1, 1], [1, 2]] sends them to (0, 0), (1, 1), (2, 3), (1, 2).",
  "The two parallelograms are different, so AB ≠ BA, but each has area 1 because det = 1."
